        ireq6->pktopts = NULL;
        if (newnp->pktoptions)
            skb_set_owner_r(newnp->pktoptions, newsk);
    }

3. Vulnerability Knowledge Mapping
a. Are there multiple concurrent system calls possible? Yes, because this is in the context of socket handling inside the Linux kernel, and the listening socket (sk) can be subject to syscalls from userland across threads/cores.
b. Is the option copying/synchronization protected? Is there any explicit locking code or serialization? No explicit locking, mutex, spinlock, or RCU use is visible in the function. This means that the critical section (copying data from listening to the child socket) could overlap with other operations on the parent socket, such as setsockopt altering options.
c. memcpy/option copy is not performed within any obvious synchronization mechanism.
d. After memcpy of struct ipv6_pinfo, pointers within the struct may now reference freed or otherwise inconsistent memory if parallel changes/cleanup occur on the parent socket.

